; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Levy C Curve
; CATEGORY: Fractals
; LEVEL:    Intermediate
; TAGS:     recursion, Levy curve, color gradient, global counter
; SUMMARY:  Draws the Levy C curve with a rainbow of colors that follows the turtle's path.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   Every straight line is replaced by two shorter lines that meet
;   at a right angle, like the two sides of a tent. Repeat that
;   fourteen times and the line grows into a lacy letter C. The pen
;   color changes slowly as the turtle walks, so you can follow the
;   order in which the curve was drawn.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run. Change the level (last line) between 1 and 14.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * the square root of 2 as a shrink factor
;   * a global counter that recursion keeps adding to
;   * turning a number into a color with SIN
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Use 60 degrees instead of 45 (and shrink by 0.577 instead).
;   * Walk the curve twice, the second time with heading + 180.
;   * Color by the level instead of by the counter.
; ============================================================

; SHADE turns the number of segments drawn so far into a color.
; Three sine waves a third of a turn apart make a smooth rainbow.
to shade :n
  localmake "a :n / 30
  setpencolor (list 128 + 127 * sin :a 128 + 127 * sin :a + 120 128 + 127 * sin :a + 240)
end

; LEVY draws the curve. At level 0 it is one segment of the rainbow.
to levy :len :level
  if :level = 0 [
    shade :drawn
    make "drawn :drawn + 1
    forward :len
    stop
  ]
  ; Two legs at right angles: each leg is the full length divided by
  ; the square root of 2, by Pythagoras.
  left 45
  levy :len / sqrt 2 :level - 1
  right 90
  levy :len / sqrt 2 :level - 1
  left 45
end

clearscreen hideturtle
setbackground [245 245 240]
setpensize 1.5
make "drawn 0
; The C bulges upward and the base line goes left to right, so
; start low and to the left.
penup setxy -150 -114 setheading 90 pendown
levy 300 14
